# Line endings, and why this file is load-bearing.
#
# RESTORED. Upstream `superpowers/.gitattributes` pinned `*.sh`, `*.cmd` and
# `hooks/session-start` to `eol=lf`. It was dropped silently during the import
# and is absent from PARITY.md — the only upstream file whose *absence* is a
# functional regression rather than a deletion decision.
#
# It matters more here than it did upstream, for two reasons:
#
#   1. `/plugins/` is GENERATED AND COMMITTED. moe-mint emits the hook wrappers
#      into it, so those bytes go through a checkout on every machine that
#      installs a plugin — including Windows ones.
#   2. `hooks/run-hook.cmd` is a cmd/bash POLYGLOT. Both interpreters parse the
#      same bytes. A CRLF checkout breaks it in BOTH: bash chokes on the
#      trailing \r, and cmd's `: << 'CMDBLOCK'` heredoc guard stops matching.
#      There is no half-working state to notice — the hook just does not run.
#
# The mechanism is Git for Windows' `core.autocrlf=true`, which many installers
# still set by default: it rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout unless told not to.
# WSL2 is the supported Windows story for now, and WSL2 clones do not hit this —
# but a clone made on the Windows side and reached through /mnt/c does, and that
# is a normal thing for someone to do by accident.
#
# Verified safe when added: `git ls-files | xargs file` found zero tracked files
# with CRLF, so normalisation is a no-op on today's tree and this can only
# prevent future damage.

# Normalise everything git detects as text; check out LF everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces on the files where a CRLF is a functional break, not cosmetic.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.cmd   text eol=lf
*.ps1   text eol=lf

# Extensionless hook scripts. The missing extension is deliberate: Claude Code's
# Windows auto-detection prepends `bash` to any command containing `.sh`, which
# would run bash twice through the wrapper. So they cannot be caught by a `*.sh`
# rule and need naming.
hooks/**            text eol=lf
packages/*/hooks/** text eol=lf
plugins/**/hooks/** text eol=lf

# Byte-frozen zones: inherited evidence, verified with `diff -r` and `shasum -c`
# and asserted by tests. `-text` means git will not normalise these under any
# setting, so no future core.autocrlf or eol config can alter a recorded
# artifact. Editing a recorded artifact is editing evidence.
packages/*/docs/history/**                  -text
packages/flight/dashboard/src/static/**     -text
packages/flight/ui/src/lib/__fixtures__/**  -text

# Licenses travel verbatim; all three inherited licenses require retaining the
# notice as-is.
LICENSE       -text
**/LICENSE    -text
**/*.LICENSE  -text

# Binary.
*.woff2 binary
*.woff  binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.so    binary
*.dylib binary
*.dll   binary
*.wasm  binary
